cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite both this repository and the upstream NVIDIA dataset."
title: "Korea Victimization-Risk Persona Benchmark (KVRB)"
abstract: >-
  A survey-anchored synthetic-persona dataset and tooling layer that augments NVIDIA
  Nemotron-Personas-Korea with crime-prevention behavioral attributes (financial vulnerability,
  digital literacy, authority deference, social isolation, prior victimization, reporting
  propensity), each anchored to Korean national surveys and validated by construction. Route-B
  adds shared-demographic conditioning and one observed within-survey joint (victimization x
  reporting). For crime-prevention research, agent-based simulation, and police-officer training.
  Contains synthetic personas only; no real victims, suspects, or PII.
